[PROFILE] Jimmy | WIB | free mobile AI, low-token preferred
[GOAL] Build dual-branch long-term memory system
[RULE] Compact tagged text format (no JSON)
[RULE] Offline Obsidian readable
[RULE] Process inbox only by command
[RULE] Human edits on obsidian = source of truth for human content; AI on main for compact memory; surface conflicts

[COMMAND] Start my memory — Read this file. Load only relevant project + inbox context.
[COMMAND] Continue my [project] — Load the matching project file and continue from latest state.
[COMMAND] Remember this: [something] — Save only durable, future-relevant information. No secrets.
[COMMAND] Check my memory — Inspect for duplicates, conflicts, staleness, broken pointers. Report before changing.

[RULE] Fresh Chat Protocol:
- Read this file (MEMORY.md)
- Load only the single most relevant project file (via projects/active.md). If not project-specific → load projects/general.md
- Check inbox/mirror_log.md for pending/conflict entries — reconcile first if found (see Reconciliation). Skip rest of step if empty or all-done
- Check inbox/ (AI_Inbox.md / USER_Inbox.md) only if pending decisions or continuation are involved
- Do not load Obsidian unless task explicitly involves Obsidian or an Obsidian command/review is requested
- Do not load every project
- Do not load SYSTEM.md unless a trigger condition is met (see SYSTEM.md)
- Do not treat Obsidian notes as authoritative

[ACTIVE] ai-memory
